applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA KOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITOH HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KISHIMOTO YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA SHIGERU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>WATANABE SHUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIKAWA, KOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITOH, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KISHIMOTO, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, SHIGERU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WATANABE, SHUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A concentrated constant irreciprocal device comprising a permanent magnet for applying a DC magnetic field to a ferrimagnetic body, an assembly in which at least a part of a plurality of center conductors one end of which serves as a common terminal and the other of which serves as a first input/output terminal is wound on or embedded in the ferrimagnetic body, a plurality of second input/output terminals, a plurality of impedance converting circuits connected between the second input/output terminals and the first input/output terminals, respectively, and a plurality of load capacitors connected between the first input/output terminals and the common terminals, respectively. The input impedance Zi of the corresponding first input/output terminal at the operating center frequency and an external impedance Zo connected with the corresponding second input/output terminal satisfy 0.05 &lt;/= Zi/Zo &lt;/= 0.9. As a result, it is possible to provide a small concentrated constant circulator/isolator of a wide band width having excellent electric characteristics.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un dispositif non réciproque, constant et concentré comprenant un aimant permanent destiné à appliquer un champ magnétique à courant continu sir un corps ferromagnétique ; un ensemble, dans lequel au moins une partie d'une pluralité de conducteurs centraux dont une extrémité sert de terminal général et l'autre extrémité de premier terminal entrée/sortie, qui est enroulé ou encastré dans le corps ferromagnétique; une pluralité de seconds terminaux entrée/sortie; une pluralité de circuits de conversion d'impédance connectés entre les seconds et les premiers terminaux entrée/sortie, respectivement; et une pluralité de condensateurs de charge connectés entre les premiers terminaux et les terminaux généraux, respectivement. L'impédance d'entrée Zi du premier terminal entrée/sortie correspondant, au niveau de la fréquence centrale de fonctionnement, et une impédance externe Zo connectée au second terminal entrée/sortie correspondant satisfont à l'équation: 0,05 &lt;/= Zi/Zo &lt;/= 0,9. En conséquence, il est possible d'obtenir un petit circulateur/isolateur d'une grande largeur de bande présentant d'excellentes caractéristiques électriques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>